{"requirements":[{"id":"containerized-webapp-runtime","requirement":"A containerized web application runs on node1 as the unprivileged appsvc account and serves on port 8080 without an active appsvc login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observations show an OCI runc container owned by appsvc, its web process running as host UID 112 with container UID/GID mappings to appsvc, distinct PID and mount namespaces, a listener on port 8080, and a successful HTTP response. appsvc had a nologin shell and zero login sessions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f76a760721344c0a","cmd-a1b22bea4dde4c5f"]},{"id":"boot-start-and-recovery","requirement":"The application starts automatically at boot while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd unit was enabled and healthy before restart. The restart was acknowledged, SSH became unavailable during the bounded reboot, the boot ID changed, and the recovered system showed the unit active, a newly created running container, a successful HTTP response, port 8080 listening, and zero appsvc login sessions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aeeed38bdc584dbf","cmd-f76a760721344c0a","cmd-5f9d208857b34636","cmd-33da09bc72aa48ac","cmd-7232b6b6e3cb4990","cmd-f4916fe1333549b0","cmd-a1b22bea4dde4c5f","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing runc, creating appsvc and its OCI bundle, and installing/enabling the systemd unit were causally necessary. The temporary manual container test provided bounded validation and was stopped and deleted before the final service was installed; its temporary log did not remain after reboot. Expected read-only SSH failures occurred only while the node rebooted. Final lifecycle checks showed healthy package state, no failed services, and no executor-created temporary-file residue beyond normal per-boot systemd artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8d52af1013764f1b","cmd-49a76ea06d4c4fe0","cmd-f70f9d0ab7df4041","cmd-7ecd8ad5e4434328","cmd-aeeed38bdc584dbf","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The application was directly shown running in an OCI container as appsvc on port 8080 without an appsvc login session, and a bounded node restart demonstrated automatic boot startup and full service recovery. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and its boot identities agree with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The later fixed lifecycle listening-socket inventory was empty and therefore did not independently corroborate port 8080, although it also omitted baseline infrastructure listeners; direct executor observations immediately after reboot showed both a successful HTTP request and the port-8080 listener."]}
